<title>FRANCE: French adj August current a/c surplus 10.4 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj August current a/c surplus 10.4 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 10.40 billion francs in August, up from a unrevised 98 million franc surplus in July, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry said the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first eight months of 1996 was 69.78 billion francs, compared with a 62.80 billion surplus in the first eight months of 1995.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					 Aug	Jul     Jun 1996</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)   10.40     0.09     9.46</p>
<p> Current account		   1.59     8.55     4.43</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 4.41     7.81     5.91</p>
<p> Services			    5.77     9.96     8.44</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.40     0.60     0.47</p>
<p> Income			     -2.15    -1.78    -2.99</p>
<p> Transfers			  -6.83    -8.04    -7.40</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					 Aug	Jul     Jun 1996</p>
<p> Current account		  10.40     0.09     9.46</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		13.11     2.78     6.58</p>
<p> Services			    6.38     7.56     6.00</p>
<p>  -Travel			    4.57     5.09     4.06</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.52     0.52     0.45</p>
<p> Income			     -4.96    -2.65    -5.35</p>
<p>  -investment income	    -3.55    -2.79    -4.64</p>
<p> Transfers			  -0.62    -0.73    -0.54</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 2441 5452</p>
</text>
